WEBVTT

00:09:57.844 --> 00:10:00.305
because you sit down
and you're struck by lightning

00:10:00.329 --> 00:10:01.745
and then you start to create.

00:10:01.769 --> 00:10:05.612
Curiosity, I think, is a far more friendly
way to do creativity than passion.

00:10:05.636 --> 00:10:09.116
CA: So, I think you yourself have done
a pretty amazing curiosity journey

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.089
in the creation of one of your novels,

00:10:11.113 --> 00:10:13.512
and you didn't even know
that it was leading there.

00:10:13.536 --> 00:10:15.738
You got curious
about gardening, of all things.

00:10:15.762 --> 00:10:16.916
EG: Yeah. (Laughs)

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:18.607
CA: Talk to us about that journey.

00:10:18.631 --> 00:10:21.140
EG: Yeah, you know,
I'm so obedient to curiosity.

00:10:21.164 --> 00:10:22.684
That's really my policy.

00:10:22.708 --> 00:10:25.949
My willingness in life is that
if inspiration comes to me

00:10:25.973 --> 00:10:27.592
in even the smallest way,

00:10:27.616 --> 00:10:30.190
I'm so respectful about seeing what it is.